WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.500
This is Kinosaki Onsen, a small hot spring
town located in Hyogo Prefecture.

00:00:05.791 --> 00:00:08.500
It is regarded as one of the best
onsen towns in Japan.

00:00:08.916 --> 00:00:11.958
As someone who's enjoyed his fair
share of onsens over the years.

00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:15.250
I was curious about Kinosaki,
so I decided to visit.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.291
Over the next two days and one night,
I'll be exploring Kinosaki Onsen.

00:00:20.291 --> 00:00:21.750
I'll be sampling local delicacies,

00:00:23.291 --> 00:00:24.666
staying at a beautiful ryokan,

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:27.791
and soaking in a breathtaking onsen.

00:00:28.375 --> 00:00:31.833
Come along as I explore Kinosaki Onsen 
and share with you

00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:35.250
why you need to visit this small but
charming hot spring town.

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:45.000
From Kyoto, it only takes
a little over two hours

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:47.916
to reach Kinosaki Onsen via direct train.

00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:52.083
We jump on a JR Limited Express
train to Kinosaki.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.000
We arrive in Kinosaki Onsen
just before noon.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.416
Our first task was to find a lunch spot,

00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:10.041
but we needed to deal with
our luggage first.

00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:15.333
We just dropped our luggage off at 
the Kinosaki Tourism Center and they'll either

00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:21.683
keep it there or transfer it to a hotel 
for a small fee of about 200 yen per bag,

00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:23.743
which is great because then 
we can just immediately

00:01:23.743 --> 00:01:26.007
 go and explore the town here.

00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:27.736
We decided to head for lunch

00:01:27.736 --> 00:01:30.083
and we found this place 
called Mikuni that specializes

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:33.854
in steak and beef, 
but specifically Tajima beef 

00:01:33.854 --> 00:01:35.696
is what we're looking for.

00:01:35.696 --> 00:01:39.666
This is sorf of the special beef 
that you can have in Kinosaki.

00:01:40.041 --> 00:01:43.458
So we just ordered a lunch set
and it came out to like a

00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:46.083
whopping 22,000 yen per person. 

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.625
So it's definitely not cheap.

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:09.166
As we continue through town, 
we start to notice more and more shops

00:02:09.291 --> 00:02:10.625
selling snow crab. 

00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:14.791
Kinosaki is especially well known for
snow crab during the winter months,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.625
thanks to its location near
the Sea of Japan.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.416
It's one of the town's 
most celebrated ingredients,

00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:23.083
and something we'll get 
more familiar with later on

00:02:29.833 --> 00:02:33.500
After lunch, we keep things light, 
picking up a few snacks as we walk,

00:02:34.166 --> 00:02:36.041
including this Strawberry Daifuku.

00:02:40.208 --> 00:02:41.083
Is it good?

00:02:42.208 --> 00:02:43.083
The strawberry is good.

00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:47.708
We also managed to grab  a box of Canelé.

00:02:58.208 --> 00:03:00.875
We begin walking along the Otani river

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.916
This is arguably the most 
picturesque part of Kinosaki.

00:03:08.666 --> 00:03:10.666
The main river runs through the town, 

00:03:10.666 --> 00:03:13.208
lined with willow trees, 
with small bridges connecting

00:03:13.208 --> 00:03:14.875
both sides of town.

00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:25.750
You'll also find plenty of shops
along the main street.

00:03:26.208 --> 00:03:29.083
It's really a pleasant area
to explore on foot.

00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:32.416
After exploring the town for a bit,

00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:34.958
we head over to our 
accommodation to check in.

00:03:35.958 --> 00:03:40.083
All right, so we just checked
in at our hotel here.

00:03:40.166 --> 00:03:41.750
I'm just going to show you guys
the room a little bit.

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:51.541
The room that we book is a sort of
Japanese traditional room

00:03:51.625 --> 00:03:53.625
with tatami floors, as you can see here.

00:03:53.916 --> 00:03:56.291
It comes with its own sort
of personal spa

00:03:56.375 --> 00:03:58.833
that we wanted for our experience here.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.291
With that said, 
we already have booked a 

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:06.875
Private onsen experience at this 
onsen sort of facility

00:04:06.958 --> 00:04:08.833
that I have on the third
floor of the hotel.

00:04:08.916 --> 00:04:12.625
I've seen photos of it, it looks really
nice, so I'm excited to try that out.

00:04:12.958 --> 00:04:15.416
But yeah, really nice hotel, feels more

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.375
glamorous than I expected really,
but looking forward

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.458
to experience everything this
hotel has to offer.

00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:24.375
It's time for onsen, so I see
you guys over there.

00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:36.559
We just arrived at our private onsen,  

00:04:36.559 --> 00:04:39.612
it's yet again a lot more than I expected.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.500
Look at this, it is beautiful.

00:05:18.041 --> 00:05:22.541
So, me and Lisa just finished our
private onsen experience.

00:05:22.833 --> 00:05:27.333
The private onsen was called Gingetsu
which is their Japanese version.

00:05:27.666 --> 00:05:29.416
They actually have two other versions, 
I believe,

00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:32.958
a Chinese version and
a Balinese version.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.620
So if you want to book 
the one that we had,

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.166
it's called Gingetsu, the Japanese one.

00:05:39.541 --> 00:05:43.083
Yeah, overall, 
it was a fantastic experience.

00:05:47.041 --> 00:05:49.125
We head out for a 
short stroll before dinner.

00:05:49.958 --> 00:05:51.666
By this time, more and more people

00:05:51.666 --> 00:05:54.500
are walking around in colorful yukatas,

00:05:54.875 --> 00:05:59.000
most likely on their way to one of 
Kinosaki's seven public bathhouses, 

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.291
one of the town's main attractions.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.541
It was now time to head
back to our ryokan

00:06:17.625 --> 00:06:21.083
to enjoy a kaiseiki dinner
served in our room.

